# SelectoComponents Shared Analytics Workbook

SelectoComponents 0.4.12 rebuilt Graph on Aggregate's analytical query shape.
Columns can now carry intrinsic `default_grouping` and `default_aggregate`
hints, while explicit domain-level defaults remain authoritative.

## Setup

```elixir
Code.require_file(Path.expand("support/bootstrap.exs", __DIR__))
SelectoLivebooksNotebookBootstrap.install_components!()
```

## 1) Put analytical intent next to each column

```elixir
analytics_domain = %{
  name: "Bookings",
  source: %{
    source_table: "bookings",
    primary_key: :id,
    fields: [:id, :booked_at, :region, :hours],
    redact_fields: [],
    columns: %{
      id: %{type: :integer},
      booked_at: %{type: :utc_datetime, default_grouping: :month},
      region: %{type: :string, default_grouping: :default},
      hours: %{type: :integer, default_aggregate: :sum}
    },
    associations: %{}
  },
  schemas: %{},
  joins: %{}
}

analytics_selecto = Selecto.configure(analytics_domain, Selecto.Runtime.Context.new(SelectoDBPostgreSQL.Adapter, :compile_only))

group_defaults = SelectoComponents.Views.Analytic.Defaults.group_by(analytics_selecto)
aggregate_defaults = SelectoComponents.Views.Analytic.Defaults.aggregate(analytics_selecto)

%{group_by: group_defaults, aggregate: aggregate_defaults}
```

## 2) Build the shared Aggregate/Graph query state

Aggregate and Graph now use identical `group_by` and `aggregate` items. Graph
adds only visual mapping. Copying an Aggregate query to Graph preserves the
filters and Graph visual configuration.

```elixir
to_items = fn defaults, prefix ->
  defaults
  |> Enum.with_index(1)
  |> Enum.map(fn {{field, config}, index} ->
    {"#{prefix}-#{index}", field, config}
  end)
end

view_config = %{
  view_mode: "aggregate",
  filters: [
    {"active-region", "filters", %{"filter" => "region", "comp" => "!=", "value" => ""}}
  ],
  views: %{
    aggregate: %{
      group_by: to_items.(group_defaults, "group"),
      aggregate: to_items.(aggregate_defaults, "aggregate")
    },
    graph: %{
      group_by: [],
      aggregate: [],
      visual: %{type: "bar", series: [], options: %{"title" => "Hours by month"}}
    }
  }
}

graph_config = SelectoComponents.Form.ParamsState.copy_aggregate_to_graph(view_config)

%{
  view_mode: graph_config.view_mode,
  filters_preserved?: graph_config.filters == view_config.filters,
  group_by: graph_config.views.graph.group_by,
  aggregate: graph_config.views.graph.aggregate,
  visual: graph_config.views.graph.visual
}
```

## 3) Override column hints at the domain level

Existing domains can continue to provide explicit lists. A non-empty explicit
list wins over the column-local hints.

```elixir
explicit_domain =
  Map.merge(analytics_domain, %{
    default_group_by: ["region"],
    default_aggregate: [{"id", %{"format" => "count"}}]
  })

explicit_selecto = Selecto.configure(explicit_domain, Selecto.Runtime.Context.new(SelectoDBPostgreSQL.Adapter, :compile_only))

%{
  group_by: SelectoComponents.Views.Analytic.Defaults.group_by(explicit_selecto),
  aggregate: SelectoComponents.Views.Analytic.Defaults.aggregate(explicit_selecto)
}
```

For overlay-authored domains, the equivalent column directives are
`default_grouping/1` and `default_aggregate/1` inside `defcolumn`.

## 4) Preserve Graph display state in URL parameters

Graph's analytical query and its visual mapping are separate, but both need to
round-trip. Current Components keeps chart type, title, axis labels, series,
and color fields in encoded URL state.

```elixir
graph_url_params =
  SelectoComponents.Form.ParamsState.view_config_to_params(graph_config)

%{
  chart_type: graph_url_params["graph_chart_type"],
  options: graph_url_params["graph_options"],
  group_by: graph_url_params["graph_group_by"],
  aggregate: graph_url_params["graph_aggregate"]
}
```

## 5) Normalize finite filter vocabularies

Fields or filters with a finite `:options` vocabulary render as selects instead
of free text. Scalars, Phoenix-style `{label, value}` tuples, and label/value
maps normalize to a single `{value, label}` shape.

```elixir
SelectoComponents.Form.FilterRendering.static_filter_options(%{
  type: :string,
  options: [
    "Ready to reserve",
    {"Needs attention", "attention"},
    %{label: "Retired", value: "retired"}
  ]
})
```
